    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0440" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg428"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.796/263a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-03-07T15:00:00-04:00">March 7, 1942—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>322. In view of Prebisch’s<anchor n="90" xml:id="d411-f1"/> statement that the
                    Argentine Government would block the proceeds of funds resulting from the
                    purchase of French ships in Argentina, as reported in the inclosure to your
                    despatch no. 4199, February 20,<anchor n="91" xml:id="d411-f2"/> the Department
                    suggests that if you perceive no objection, you endeavor to persuade the
                    authorities to <pb facs="0441" n="429" xml:id="pg429"/> block the proceeds
                    should Argentina purchase planes and spare parts from Air France.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d411-f1" n="90" xml:id="d411-f1-content">
                <p>Raúl Prebisch, General Manager of the Banco Central de la República
                    Argentina.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d411-f2" n="91" xml:id="d411-f2-content">
                <p>Despatch No. 4199 not printed, but for memorandum of February 20, by the Second
                    Secretary of Embassy in Argentina, enclosed in the despatch, see <ref
                        target="#pg455">p. 455</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
